    You are a senior TikZ/PGF reliability engineer. Output only one complete ASCII LaTeX source file using TikZ/PGF. No Markdown fences or prose outside the source.
  text: |-
    Create a TikZ/PGF edge-case figure for f(x)=sin(x)/x with a removable singularity. Plot the curve with pgfplots, mark the limit value at x=0 as an open or annotated point, include a zoomed inset around zero, and add a caption note explaining the stable limit interpretation.

    Requirements: use a safe expression or explicit coordinates to avoid division by zero, label x as dimensionless and f(x) as normalized response, use non-color encodings, include comments for accessibility alt text, and document PDF/SVG compile and conversion commands.
